**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialSourcesWindowTests`

**How to implement.** The Online sources window: single-instance, fitted to its screen and reachable at small sizes (.spec-md §4 'UI': every new window calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen` and joins `ScrollExtentTests`; §10.1; the S13.1 brief: ids, keepOnScreen, ScrollExtentTests). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Online sources group (step 450): `materialSourcesWindow` (`"MaterialSourcesWindow"`) with a one-line doc. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/WindowLauncher.fs`: `WindowKey` (`WindowLauncher.fs:34`) gains `MaterialSourcesWindowKey`, documented in one line: the single-instance Online sources window. (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialSourcesWindow.fs` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui`, compiled directly after `MaterialSourcesView.fs` (step 450) and before `MaterialsWindow.fs`: one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `type MaterialSourcesWindow(imports : CatalogueImportContext, pullsApplied : ControlCaption -> unit)` inherits `HostWindow`, is titled `Online sources`, carries `materialSourcesWindow` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`, opens at 720 × 640 and calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen` (`OpticalConstructor.Controls/WindowLayout.fs`). It captures the Elmish dispatch from its init command as `MaterialsWindow` does (`MaterialsWindow.fs:35`) and runs `Program.mkProgram` over `initMaterialSources`, `updateMaterialSources` and `materialSourcesView` with the context `{ imports = imports; jobs = SourceSnapshotJobHost.onUiThread (SourceSnapshotProgressed >> dispatch) (SourceSnapshotEnded >> dispatch); pullsApplied = pullsApplied }` (step 450). Its `Closed` hook dispatches `CancelSourceSnapshot`, so a closed window leaves no update running. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs`: `rootWindowFactory` (`WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs:44`), exhaustive over `WindowKey`, answers `MaterialSourcesWindowKey` with `MaterialSourcesWindow(ctx.catalogueImports, ignore)`, as step 190 gave it `KitWindowKey`; its facts keep their names, keys and assertions, the window being rendered by its own ui-smoke fact below. (5) Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs` gains `the Online sources window leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable "OnlineSources"` (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:89`) over a `MaterialSourcesWindow` whose import context, `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy` with `materialSources` set by record update, offers step 443's double holding a snapshot, and whose `pullsApplied` ignores its caption. New `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialSourcesWindowTests.fs`, `module MaterialSourcesWindowTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment: its windows are built over that import context, the double holding the Silicon record (`main/Si/nk/Aspnes.yml`, `Si (Silicon), Aspnes`) at `2026-11-01`, and a recording `pullsApplied`, shown headless at 800 × 600 as `DataLocationsWindowTests` shows its window (step 193). Without a trait: `the Online sources UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the texts of `materialSourcesWindow` and of step 450's nine fixed ids, and `materialSourceChoice` of `Test source`, `materialSourceHitRow` and `materialSourcePullButton` of `main/Si/nk/Aspnes.yml`. `the Online sources window is titled, carries its id and lists its source with its snapshot`: the window is titled `Online sources` and carries `materialSourcesWindow` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`; `materialSourceChoice` of `Test source` exists; and `materialSourceSnapshotText` reads `Snapshot 2026-11-01`. `a window with no source says so and offers nothing`: over `CatalogueImportContext.create`'s `[]`, `materialSourcesStatusText` reads `No online material source is configured.` and no `materialSourceUpdateButton` or `materialSourceQueryBox` exists. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing a box at its centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` does: `pressing Search then Pull pulls the record and tells the opener`: with `materialSourceQueryBox`'s text set to `silicon`, pressing `materialSourceSearchButton` shows `materialSourceHitRow` of the Silicon record, and pressing its `materialSourcePullButton` records `Pulled Si (Silicon), Aspnes as version 1.` through `pullsApplied` and shows it in `materialSourcesStatusText`. `the Online sources window opens once through the registry`: two `openOrActivate MaterialSourcesWindowKey` through `WindowLauncher.create` over a factory building the window answer one live window, as step 194's Data locations fact does. No fact presses Update snapshot over a real downloader.

**Acceptance.** After the window lands, `MaterialSourcesWindow` MUST be titled `Online sources`, carry its id, keep on screen, open single-instance under `MaterialSourcesWindowKey` and cancel a running update when it closes; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Search then Pull pulls the record and tells the opener` and `the Online sources window opens once through the registry`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Online sources window leaves everything reachable`, `the Online sources UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the Online sources window is titled, carries its id and lists its source with its snapshot` and `a window with no source says so and offers nothing`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s43 invariants MUST pass.
